      "doctor_question": "Hi, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S001",
      "patient_response": "Hi. Yeah, um, well... what finally scared me into coming in is that I just keep making these really dumb technical mistakes at work. And I know better! I'm an editor and a camera operator, so I've been doing this a long time. Actually, I just got off this massive reality TV shoot last week—we were out in the middle of nowhere for like four days, and the catering was just awful. Honestly, it was just stale bagels and lukewarm coffee, which I really can't stand because I need my coffee piping hot, you know? My sister used to work at a coffee shop and she always told me the secret to a good brew is... wait, what was I saying? \n\nOh, right, why I'm here. Yeah, so I'm doing things like labeling camera cards wrong, or completely missing a timecode note. The worst is when I export a client cut with the wrong lower-third graphic on the screen... and that's even after I’ve checked it! It's just getting really embarrassing and I'm scared it's going to cost me my job.",
