      "doctor_question": "When you were a child, did you often have trouble paying attention or staying organized?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, yeah, absolutely. It's funny you ask about childhood because my mom just found this huge box of my old report cards when she was cleaning out the garage. She’s trying to downsize, you know? She wants to move to this condo near the beach, which is great, but the HOA fees are just insane. I told her she should look a little further inland, but she loves the ocean. Anyway, those report cards... yeah, it was always the same thing. Even in elementary school, they were always moving my desk right up next to the teacher's. I was just constantly out of my seat, or I'd just blurt out the answers before anyone else could, or I'd be poking or talking to whoever was sitting next to me. Half the time I didn't even realize I was doing it until the teacher yelled at me.",
