    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have these focus and organization problems been present pretty much your whole adult life?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, um... not my whole adult life, no. I mean, I've always been a little scattered, but it really hasn't been this bad until, gosh, about two years and two months ago? Yeah, that sounds right. That's when my company went through this massive readjustment. They totally changed how our shoots are scheduled and how the edit reviews run. It used to be this really collaborative thing where we'd all sit in the editing bay, and my old producer, Dave—oh my gosh, Dave was the best. He had this vintage popcorn machine in his office, like an actual movie theater one, and he'd make popcorn for every single review session. The whole hallway smelled like butter on Thursdays. He retired to Maine, actually. Bought a boat, which I am so jealous of. I’ve always wanted to learn how to sail, but the knots seem really complicated. \n\nBut yeah, since the readjustment, everything is just... different. It's been going on at this super disruptive level ever since they changed the workflow. I just can't seem to keep up with the new system.",
